cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RBACO-BFO, please cite it with these metadata."
title: "RBACO-BFO: Role-Based Access Control Ontology, BFO edition"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
abstract: >-
  An ontology of role-based access control on BFO 2020, the Common Core Ontologies v2.2 and IAO. It
  re-expresses the patterns of ROWLBAC (Finin et al., SACMAT 2008) to the semantics of the proposed NIST
  RBAC standard (Ferraiolo et al., ACM TISSEC 2001), with tasks and separation of duty after Botha and
  Eloff (IBM Systems Journal 2001), and comes with first-order axioms in CLIF, SPARQL derivations and
  checks, example data, and the records of how it was verified.
